 # 16\. Audit log integrity

 Your repository already has an audit trail concept.

 Strengthen it.

 Instead of:

```
timestamp
event
```

 consider an append-only integrity model:

```
event_n
   +
hash(event_n)
   +
previous_event_hash
        ↓
event_n_hash
```

 Conceptually:

```
Event 1 → H1
Event 2 + H1 → H2
Event 3 + H2 → H3
Event 4 + H3 → H4
```

 Then modification of an old event breaks the chain.

 Test:

```
change event 1
→ chain verification fails

change event 50
→ chain verification fails

delete event
→ chain verification fails

reorder events
→ chain verification fails
```

 For high-assurance environments, consider authenticated storage or external immutable/WORM-style archival rather than relying solely on a local hash chain.

