 # 28\. GitHub Actions hardening

 This is a **major attack surface**.

 Review every workflow.

 For each workflow:

```
permissions:
  contents: read
```

 Then grant only the permissions actually needed.

 Do not casually use:

```
permissions: write-all
```

 or equivalent broad privileges.

 Also:

```
pin third-party actions
review action updates
avoid untrusted PR code accessing secrets
separate deployment workflows
use environments
require approvals
```

 GitHub specifically warns about workflow security and provides artifact attestations and OIDC as hardening mechanisms.  GitHub Docs

---

 # 29\. Never expose production secrets to ordinary PRs

 Especially important for public repositories.

 The model should be:

```
Public PR
   ↓
tests
   ↓
NO production secrets
```

 Production deployment:

```
trusted branch
+
trusted workflow
+
environment approval
+
short-lived credentials
```

 A malicious PR must never be able to print your exchange key simply by modifying a test.

