 # 42\. Trading invariants

 Now back to software correctness.

 I would establish a formal invariant suite:

```
INV-001
No order exceeds configured maximum notional.

INV-002
No new entry is allowed while capital-preservation halt is active.

INV-003
Unknown exchange order state cannot become FILLED without reconciliation.

INV-004
NaN/Infinity cannot produce an executable order.

INV-005
A disabled trading mode cannot submit orders.

INV-006
Risk engine failure cannot result in an executable order.

INV-007
Duplicate execution requests cannot create unintended duplicate positions.

INV-008
A stale market-data sample cannot be treated as current without explicit policy.

INV-009
Position/account state after restart must reconcile with exchange state.

INV-010
Live mode cannot bypass qualification gates.
```

 These become **non-negotiable tests**.

