 # 58\. Five-whys example

 Suppose duplicate orders occurred.

```
Why?
Two execution requests were processed.

Why?
No idempotency key.

Why?
Executor assumed requests were serialized.

Why?
Architecture didn't enforce idempotency.

Why?
Requirement didn't specify duplicate-request behavior.
```

 The solution isn't merely:

```
"be careful"
```

 It becomes:

```
idempotency requirement
+
implementation
+
unit test
+
concurrency test
+
regression test
+
architecture rule
```

 That's continuous improvement.

